WEBVTT

00:05.380 --> 00:05.834
[CARLA]
Eren--

00:06.837 --> 00:08.110
You want them to think
that you're strong?

00:08.675 --> 00:09.333
Exercise restraint.

00:10.050 --> 00:11.970
Try protecting Mikasa
once in a while.

00:13.000 --> 00:15.925
[EREN]
Stop it! No!

00:23.640 --> 00:27.640
[Gasps]

01:27.700 --> 01:32.670
♪ Opening Song ♪

02:16.650 --> 02:18.310
He tossing Titans now?

02:18.350 --> 02:21.720
That son of a bitch
has gone berserk!

02:21.750 --> 02:24.550
[REINER TITAN roars]

02:24.590 --> 02:26.120
[JEAN grunts]

02:36.100 --> 02:38.200
[YMIR]
Damn you, Commander Erwin!

02:38.230 --> 02:40.170
I had this all planned out.

02:40.200 --> 02:42.670
Why'd you have to go
and screw it up?

02:42.700 --> 02:44.000
[Gasps]

02:50.150 --> 02:52.780
[CHRISTA]
Ymir! Conny! Over there!

02:52.810 --> 02:54.210
I see!

02:57.020 --> 02:59.720
Commander!

02:59.760 --> 03:01.920
[ERWIN]
I'm not your objective.

03:01.960 --> 03:05.630
Don't waste time on
someone who's replaceable.

03:05.660 --> 03:07.590
Retrieve Eren and go.

03:07.630 --> 03:09.860
[MALE SOLDIER 37A screams]

03:20.140 --> 03:22.010
[MIKASA]
Get down!

03:23.650 --> 03:26.180
[HANNES grunts]

03:26.210 --> 03:28.380
Are you insane?

03:28.850 --> 03:31.150
[Yells]

03:33.690 --> 03:34.720
[Laughs]

03:34.760 --> 03:36.390
Can you believe this luck?

03:36.430 --> 03:39.060
Ha! Crazy, right?

03:39.090 --> 03:42.400
Watch me! This is the least
that I owe your mother.

03:42.430 --> 03:46.000
She'll finally have
the vengeance she deserves!

03:46.070 --> 03:47.730
[Yells]

03:48.900 --> 03:51.200
No! Hannes!

03:51.240 --> 03:53.310
[JEAN]
He needs backup!

03:57.110 --> 03:58.810
[ARMIN yells]

04:01.720 --> 04:03.980
[ARMIN]
Reiner. What the--?

04:04.020 --> 04:06.990
Doesn't he care
if Eren gets eaten?

04:07.020 --> 04:08.860
Move it or lose it, asshole!

04:08.890 --> 04:11.260
I'm tired of your shit!

04:18.800 --> 04:21.770
What are you doing?

04:21.800 --> 04:24.800
[YMIR]
Honestly? Hell if I know.

04:24.840 --> 04:27.710
Do I trust Reiner,
or gamble on the Scouts

04:27.740 --> 04:29.380
and hope for the best?

04:29.440 --> 04:31.010
[Grunts]

04:32.380 --> 04:36.180
[YMIR] Suppose I actually
manage to live through this.

04:36.220 --> 04:39.790
What good's another day
on borrowed time?

04:39.820 --> 04:42.160
Life inside the walls
will be a nightmare.

04:42.190 --> 04:44.220
That's a fact.

04:44.260 --> 04:46.360
This may be my only shot
at bringing her over

04:46.390 --> 04:50.260
to the other side.
I'm just one person.

04:50.300 --> 04:52.830
I can't protect her forever.

04:57.210 --> 04:58.810
Christa!

04:58.840 --> 05:00.970
No. No more.

05:01.010 --> 05:04.340
Sorry, from now on
I'm Historia.

05:04.380 --> 05:07.410
Okay, so tell me.

05:07.450 --> 05:11.820
What did you mean exactly
by "handing me over"?

05:11.850 --> 05:15.990
Would it really have saved you,
or was that a lie?

05:16.020 --> 05:20.190
Stupid question.
Of course it was.

05:20.230 --> 05:24.160
Why, then?
Why go to the trouble?

05:27.540 --> 05:30.340
Was it me?

05:30.370 --> 05:33.110
You were trying
to protect me again!

05:33.840 --> 05:35.340
[CONNY]
Heads up!

05:37.980 --> 05:41.280
Listen to me. You need
to take your own advice.

05:41.320 --> 05:44.250
You understand me?

05:44.290 --> 05:46.990
Stop putting
yourself on the line!

05:47.020 --> 05:52.090
You need to live your
own life! Live it with me!

05:52.130 --> 05:54.030
I never told you this before,

05:54.060 --> 05:58.130
but however bad things get,
as long as we're together...

05:58.170 --> 06:00.270
...I'm not afraid!

06:08.440 --> 06:11.780
[Yells]

06:11.810 --> 06:13.950
[Yells]

06:20.120 --> 06:24.520
[EREN] Mikasa, stop!
You're in no shape to--!

06:24.560 --> 06:26.230
My hands! Help me!

06:26.260 --> 06:27.460
What'll you do?

06:27.500 --> 06:29.430
[EREN]
Come on!

06:29.460 --> 06:32.230
I have to be the one
who kills that thing!

06:32.300 --> 06:33.800
[Grunts]

06:33.840 --> 06:36.200
I ain't done with you yet!

06:37.440 --> 06:40.040
This one belongs to me!
Wait here.

06:40.080 --> 06:45.110
Eren! Don't go! We have to
get you out of here!

06:45.150 --> 06:49.120
Not until I've settled
the score. Stand back.

06:54.990 --> 06:56.420
[Gasps]

06:57.560 --> 06:59.160
[EREN]
What?

06:59.190 --> 07:01.490
[MALE SOLDIER 37B yells]

07:04.630 --> 07:06.270
[MALE SOLDIER 37C]
Commander!

07:06.300 --> 07:08.970
Sir! The Armored!

07:09.000 --> 07:11.040
It's coming this way!

07:14.040 --> 07:16.280
[Gasps]
Jean!

07:16.310 --> 07:19.250
[JEAN grunts]

07:19.280 --> 07:20.480
[Groans]

07:20.520 --> 07:23.850
[ARMIN]
No!

07:23.890 --> 07:28.190
Oh god. Stay with me, Jean!

07:28.260 --> 07:30.490
[Yells]

07:32.260 --> 07:36.930
[EREN]
No! Don't do this!

07:36.970 --> 07:38.500
Not now!

07:42.070 --> 07:43.900
Eren, stop!

07:43.940 --> 07:49.440
[EREN growls]

07:49.480 --> 07:54.250
[ARMIN yells]

07:57.150 --> 07:59.020
[Yells]

08:01.220 --> 08:05.290
[PEER screams]
Commander!

08:06.630 --> 08:09.130
[Yells]

08:17.140 --> 08:19.470
[Gasps]

08:19.510 --> 08:21.040
[Gasps]

08:24.380 --> 08:25.680
[HANNES screams]

08:25.710 --> 08:31.450
[EREN] Come on!
Transform, goddamn it!

08:31.490 --> 08:34.290
Don't let this be for nothing!

08:34.320 --> 08:37.660
[HANNES screams, muffled]

08:37.690 --> 08:39.930
[Squelch]

09:04.350 --> 09:09.990
[Sobs]

09:10.030 --> 09:16.600
[Laughs intensely]

09:16.630 --> 09:19.030
[MIKASA]
Eren.

09:19.100 --> 09:20.530
[EREN]
Look at you.

09:20.570 --> 09:24.340
You haven't grown up
one goddamn bit!

09:24.370 --> 09:29.210
You're still as useless
as you've ever been!

09:29.240 --> 09:32.550
Nothing's changed!

09:32.580 --> 09:38.990
[Sobs and  yells]

09:42.260 --> 09:47.230
I'm sorry, Mother.
I still can't do anything.

09:47.260 --> 09:51.660
No matter how hard I try,
I'm just a worthless little kid.

09:51.700 --> 09:53.470
[MIKASA]
Eren.

10:00.180 --> 10:03.040
Stop. That isn't true.

10:22.260 --> 10:26.800
[MIKASA]
Hey. Thank you.

10:26.840 --> 10:34.040
I've been meaning
to tell you that.

10:34.080 --> 10:38.180
For fighting.
For always standing by me.

10:38.210 --> 10:40.450
Thank you.

10:43.490 --> 10:45.220
For pushing through.

10:45.250 --> 10:49.160
For showing me
how to live with purpose.

10:49.190 --> 10:51.690
I'm grateful.

10:56.360 --> 10:58.300
My scarf.

11:01.240 --> 11:03.570
For always
wrapping it around me.

11:03.610 --> 11:05.740
Thank you.

11:22.860 --> 11:24.690
[EREN sniffs]

11:27.860 --> 11:34.570
[EREN] Mikasa. I will
always wrap your scarf.

11:34.600 --> 11:39.140
Always and forever.
That's a promise!

11:41.910 --> 11:46.510
[Yells]

11:53.790 --> 11:55.720
[EREN growls]

12:01.160 --> 12:05.360
[Bellows]

12:20.350 --> 12:21.810
[ARMIN]
Huh?

12:40.500 --> 12:43.600
Why're they--?
What's going on?

12:43.640 --> 12:45.810
They're eating it!

12:51.310 --> 12:53.580
Don't know,
don't care. Let's go!

12:53.620 --> 12:54.810
Could be our only chance!

12:54.850 --> 12:56.280
Right!

12:56.320 --> 12:58.380
[YMIR]
That's what this is about.

12:58.420 --> 13:01.850
No wonder Reiner was desperate
to get his hands on him.

13:01.890 --> 13:05.490
Maybe there is
a future inside the walls.

13:05.530 --> 13:07.590
I'll be damned.

13:11.370 --> 13:15.900
[REINER] This isn't good. Why'd
things have to be this way?

13:15.940 --> 13:19.340
Why'd the Coordinate
have to fall to him?

13:19.370 --> 13:22.540
Unless we can get it back,
we're finished.

13:22.580 --> 13:24.480
No two ways about it.

13:24.510 --> 13:28.210
Of all the people in the world
that power could've gone to,

13:28.250 --> 13:31.580
Eren is by far the worst.

13:31.620 --> 13:34.290
Get away from us!

13:34.320 --> 13:38.690
Rat bastards! I'll kill you
where you stand!

13:45.870 --> 13:49.870
[REINER]
Son of a bitch. Bertholdt!

13:49.900 --> 13:51.940
I can't protect him like this!

13:51.970 --> 13:53.940
What the hell is going on?

13:53.980 --> 13:56.340
[ARMIN]
Eren!

13:56.380 --> 13:57.280
Can you ride?

13:57.310 --> 13:58.810
[EREN]
Yeah!

13:58.850 --> 14:00.980
Then hurry!

14:01.020 --> 14:05.320
This may be our only window!
Soldiers, retreat!

14:09.520 --> 14:11.920
[Yells]

14:13.760 --> 14:15.260
[CHRISTA]
What is it?

14:15.300 --> 14:17.330
Hey, ugly!
Get with the program!

14:17.370 --> 14:19.530
We were given an order!

14:29.580 --> 14:32.780
Please forgive me.

14:32.810 --> 14:34.710
[Gasps]

14:39.490 --> 14:41.420
Wait! What are you doing?

14:41.460 --> 14:44.320
--Let her go!
--But she'll be killed!

14:45.790 --> 14:47.830
[Yells]

14:47.860 --> 14:51.330
[Roars]

14:51.370 --> 15:05.380
♪

15:05.410 --> 15:06.710
[ARMIN]
At the time,

15:06.750 --> 15:09.820
Ymir's decision to turn
back puzzled me,

15:09.850 --> 15:11.720
though I suspected it had
something to do with

15:11.750 --> 15:15.090
why the Armored Titan
didn't give chase.

15:15.120 --> 15:25.130
♪

15:48.380 --> 15:52.450
[Distant panting]

15:52.490 --> 15:56.590
[ALL panting]

15:56.630 --> 15:58.230
[REINER]
I don't get it.

15:58.260 --> 16:00.690
What the hell
possessed you to come back?

16:00.730 --> 16:03.830
Uh. Can't say, really.

16:03.870 --> 16:06.300
Probably wasn't
the smartest thing.

16:06.340 --> 16:08.270
Seemed a little unfair
to send you guys home

16:08.300 --> 16:13.810
empty-handed. Just, think of
me as a consolation prize.

16:13.840 --> 16:16.510
Are you serious?

16:16.550 --> 16:18.580
[YMIR] Look at it this way,
if you hadn't come

16:18.610 --> 16:20.450
to bust up the wall,

16:20.480 --> 16:23.880
who knows when my
nightmare would've ended?

16:23.920 --> 16:26.820
I owed quite a debt.

16:26.860 --> 16:31.690
This is me giving back
what I took from you.

16:31.730 --> 16:34.630
'Least somebody knows
the shit you've been through.

16:34.660 --> 16:37.300
Even if it is only me.

16:38.570 --> 16:44.640
Yeah, well...
thank you. Sorry.

16:44.670 --> 16:46.670
No worries.

16:49.750 --> 16:54.250
Being a goddess had
its perks while it lasted.

16:58.350 --> 17:00.220
[NARRATOR] With reports
maintaining the likelihood

17:00.260 --> 17:02.790
of Wall Rose
having been compromised,

17:02.830 --> 17:05.460
citizens of the region
were forced to take refuge

17:05.490 --> 17:09.430
in a subterranean city within
the confines of Wall Sina.

17:09.470 --> 17:11.730
However, though
emergency provisions

17:11.770 --> 17:13.970
had been stockpiled
for the purpose,

17:14.000 --> 17:16.840
with over half the
population relying on them,

17:16.870 --> 17:20.540
rations could only last,
at most, a week.

17:20.580 --> 17:23.010
Beyond that
lurked a terrible choice:

17:23.050 --> 17:25.250
turn on each other like animals,

17:25.280 --> 17:28.350
or face the prospect
of starvation.

17:28.380 --> 17:32.390
To avoid a humanitarian crisis
of catastrophic proportions,

17:32.420 --> 17:34.520
within a week of
the Titan onslaught,

17:34.560 --> 17:38.260
authorities declared
Wall Rose secure.

17:45.700 --> 17:48.770
[Knock, knock, knock]

17:48.800 --> 17:51.710
Hange. Come in.

17:51.740 --> 17:54.410
Pardon the intrusion, Erwin.

17:56.010 --> 17:58.850
Commander Pyxis.
Glad we caught you.

17:58.880 --> 18:00.410
[doorknob clicks, thuds]

18:00.450 --> 18:02.780
Um, this is...
State your name.

18:02.820 --> 18:04.620
Sir! Conny Springer, sir!

18:04.650 --> 18:06.620
Hundred and fourth Cadet Corps!

18:06.660 --> 18:10.390
Conny here is
originally from Ragako.

18:10.430 --> 18:13.730
Ah, yes. Where the invasion
seems to have begun, correct?

18:13.760 --> 18:17.360
[HANGE] Yes, sir.
In fact, he's corroborated

18:17.400 --> 18:19.970
a valuable piece of evidence
in that regard.

18:20.000 --> 18:23.500
I think you'll find his story
supports our hypothesis.

18:23.540 --> 18:25.940
Soldier, if you would.

18:30.110 --> 18:34.420
[EREN] I allowed myself to be
kidnapped. It's my fault.

18:34.450 --> 18:35.980
Because of me
the Scouts lost over

18:36.020 --> 18:39.720
half of their
veteran contingent.

18:39.760 --> 18:44.060
All in a single
rescue attempt.

18:44.090 --> 18:48.330
Still, though. There were no
causalities on the way back.

18:48.360 --> 18:50.560
The Titans
completely ignored us.

18:50.600 --> 18:53.930
They were too fixated
on Reiner and the others.

18:53.970 --> 18:57.840
Jean and I, we mulled it over
between us once we got back.

18:57.870 --> 18:59.840
[EREN]
Huh?

18:59.880 --> 19:04.080
Hear me out.
Suppose they acted that way...

19:04.110 --> 19:05.710
...because of you?

19:05.750 --> 19:07.680
[EREN gasps]

19:07.720 --> 19:11.020
[JEAN]
Just a thought, of course.

19:11.050 --> 19:13.420
But as far as
an explanation,

19:13.490 --> 19:16.490
it's about as good as we've got.

19:17.460 --> 19:19.960
I'm not saying I envy
the position you're in.

19:20.000 --> 19:23.660
Maybe all those people
really did die for nothing.

19:23.700 --> 19:26.670
That all depends on you.

19:26.700 --> 19:28.870
If you're really
worth the sacrifice,

19:28.900 --> 19:32.410
you'd better prove it.

19:32.440 --> 19:35.540
There's no time
for second-guessing.

19:39.780 --> 19:44.550
You're right.
I have to be decisive.

19:44.590 --> 19:48.890
If this is real--
if I can control Titans--

19:48.920 --> 19:51.430
I have to plug up Wall Maria.

19:51.460 --> 19:54.830
Then make Reiner answer
for what he's done.

19:54.860 --> 19:59.630
People died for me. I have
to earn what they gave.

20:01.640 --> 20:04.400
[PYXIS]
Come again?

20:04.440 --> 20:07.510
You're saying the
Titans responsible for this

20:07.540 --> 20:11.550
were the citizens of Ragako?

20:11.580 --> 20:18.020
I see. So, in actuality,
Titans are human beings.

20:20.760 --> 20:24.190
Well, we don't have proof yet.

20:24.230 --> 20:27.430
[LEVI]
Great. Perfect.

20:27.460 --> 20:31.730
I've spent all this time.
All this energy.

20:31.770 --> 20:35.040
And the things I've been
carving through like carrion

20:35.070 --> 20:37.700
were people.

20:37.740 --> 20:40.840
Look, we don't know
for a certainty.

20:46.120 --> 20:47.920
[CONNY sniffs]

20:51.590 --> 20:55.890
Now what?

20:55.930 --> 20:59.190
Um, excuse me.

20:59.230 --> 21:01.760
What's with that smile?

21:05.670 --> 21:07.870
Oh, it's nothing.

21:09.840 --> 21:14.740
Just... seems to me
we've taken one more step

21:14.780 --> 21:17.710
toward the truth.

21:17.750 --> 21:20.080
Wow. One whole step, huh?

21:20.120 --> 21:21.720
At this pace
we'll run out of people

21:21.750 --> 21:23.750
before we actually reach it.

21:23.790 --> 21:26.590
Not a good rate of return.

21:26.620 --> 21:29.890
Everything comes at a price.

21:29.930 --> 21:33.860
One day we'll get close
enough to break through.

21:33.900 --> 21:39.600
The wall barring us
from the truth will tumble.

22:08.100 --> 22:10.200
Not just yet.

22:10.230 --> 22:15.240
♪ Closing Song
